  "notes": "Clean review: 40/40 manifest files read in full, no partners. Security-relevant surfaces in this chunk that are already in known.json and therefore not re-reported: settings.json removal of the acdsl Edit/Write ask rules (known #10), acdsl-policy-guard path-normalization bypass (known #161), nightly additionalDirectories append from repos.json (known #8), bootstrap overwrite of .claude/settings.local.json (known #1), install.env unquoted home values (known #156). Examined and rejected (no new security boundary or not quantifiable): install.env sourced as shell by install.sh/sync_settings.sh (same-user file in a checkout the agent can already edit scripts in); peek /healthz identity check trusts self-reported homes (strict improvement over the old blind reuse; peek HTTP and OTLP control port being unauthenticated loopback listeners pre-date this diff, agent sessions use peek over stdio per settings/claude_code/claude.json); bootstrap results file at ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} (symlink/world-readable exposure only if TMPDIR is unset for the launchd configserver child, not provable here); skill-invoke-gate/read-gate are agent-conduct gates, not security boundaries; CI peek-mcp.exe download without checksum is a pre-existing pattern, only the tag changed. Cross-chunk for the station: (a) casual audience now defaults run.sh to orchestrate=1 plus auto_apply=decide, so mined proposals can reach main and be deployed by the orchestrate stage's settings sync without a human vote; whether the decide rules-file blocks permissions-kind proposals lives in skills/smine/smine-apply (other chunk, adjacent to known #5). (b) worktree-sessionstart.sh and verdict.sh now treat .serena/ as disposable infra (rm -rf of hollow pool dirs holding only .serena; removal gate ignores .serena/ contents) — data-integrity, not security.",
